<section>

    <h2>📅 Timeline</h2>

    <ol>

        <li>
            <strong>1940s</strong>
            <p>
                Early electronic computers were developed.
            </p>
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>1950s</strong>
            <p>
                Computers became increasingly important
                for scientific and business applications.
            </p>
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>1970s</strong>
            <p>
                Microprocessors helped drive the development
                of smaller computing systems.
            </p>
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>1980s</strong>
            <p>
                Personal computers became more widely used.
            </p>
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>1990s</strong>
            <p>
                The World Wide Web expanded access to online
                information.
            </p>
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>2000s</strong>
            <p>
                Smartphones and cloud-based services became
                increasingly influential.
            </p>
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>2020s</strong>
            <p>
                AI, cloud computing and advanced digital
                services continue to develop.
            </p>
        </li>

    </ol>

</section>

